course: dictionary
lesson: 13268
title: Goldsmith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A goldsmith is a person who makes things out of gold. Look at the word's parts: gold is the shiny yellow metal, and smith is a worker who makes things. A blacksmith works with iron, and a goldsmith works with gold.
explain: Read this: «The goldsmith hammered a thin gold ring.» The words around goldsmith show what the worker is doing: hammering a gold ring. Try your meaning in the sentence: a person who makes things out of gold fits, so you have understood it.
explain: Long ago, goldsmiths did more than make jewellery. «The goldsmith locked the coins in his strong box and lent money to the merchant.» This clue shows that a goldsmith could also keep gold safe and lend money, which helped start the first banks.
fact: A goldsmith is a person who makes jewellery, cups, plates and other objects out of gold.
fact: Long ago, goldsmiths also kept people's gold safe and lent money, which helped start the first banks.
fact: «Goldsmith» is a noun, and «goldsmiths» is the plural: «Two goldsmiths worked in the same street.»
fact: In London, goldsmiths' receipts were an early form of paper money.
fact: Goldsmiths made crowns, coins and church treasures, like the Anglo-Saxon gold found at Sutton Hoo.
exercise: «The goldsmith made a gold crown for the queen.» What is a goldsmith? | *A person who makes things out of gold | A person who sells fish at the market | A worker who builds stone walls | A king who wears a crown
exercise: «The goldsmith kept the villagers' gold safe in his strong room.» What else did goldsmiths do long ago? | Rode horses to London every day | Grew wheat and barley on farms | Painted pictures on church walls | *Kept gold safe and lent money
exercise: «Two goldsmiths worked all day in the workshop.» Find and copy the word that names the workers. | jewel | workshop | strong | *goldsmiths
test: «The goldsmith polished the gold cup until it shone.» What does goldsmith mean? | *A person who makes things out of gold | A person who sells fish | A cup made of wood | A person who bakes bread
test: Mia says goldsmiths only made jewellery. Is she right? | Yes, that is all they ever did | No, they made bread for the town | *No, they also made cups and plates, and long ago they kept gold safe and lent money | Yes, but only for kings
exam: «Long ago, the goldsmith's strong box held coins for the town, and people paid him to keep them safe.» What was one job of a goldsmith long ago? | To bake bread for the town | *To keep people's gold safe and lend money | To ride a horse in races | To plant trees in the park
